Building from source
====================

Dependencies
------------

* a C++23 compiler (g++ or clang++)
* CMake 3.24 or newer
* SDL 3
* libmikmod (plays the music)
* pkg-config
* make (optional, see below)

On macOS with Homebrew:

$ brew install cmake sdl3 libmikmod pkg-config

Build procedure
---------------

$ make
$ make run
$ make install

The Makefile is a thin wrapper around CMake. The equivalent CMake
commands are:

$ cmake -S . -B build
$ cmake --build build
$ cmake --install build

The game and fokker.dks end up in build/, together with the tools:

* lvledit   level editor (keys are listed in doc/lvledit-keys.txt)
* pgdview   lists or shows the pictures in fokker.dks
            (pgdview fokker [picturename])
* pcx2pgd   PCX to .pgd converter, used by tools/build-data-from-source

DESTDIR and PREFIX are supported. See doc/mingw32.txt for Windows
build instructions.

Debian packging
---------------

$ dpkg-buildpackage -rfakeroot -b

Resulting .deb package is located in parent directory.

Testsuite
---------

"make test" replays the recorded games in triplane-testsuite/ with your
build and with a baseline commit, and compares the checksum of every
frame. Any change in what the game does or draws shows up, with the
first frame where the two builds differ. Crashes and hangs fail too.

$ make test                  # working tree against the last commit
$ make test BASE=master      # against another commit, branch or tag

The baseline is built once per commit under build/baseline/. It has to
be buildable with CMake and SDL3. See tools/compare-baseline -h for the
remaining options, such as the number of frames compared per game.

"make smoke" only replays the recorded games with your build and checks
that each draws frames and ends without a crash; it needs no baseline.

GitHub Actions (.github/workflows/ci.yml) runs the build, the smoke test
and the baseline comparison against the previous commit on Linux
(Debian trixie), macOS and Windows (MSYS2) for every push and pull
request.

Regenerating data/
------------------

It is possible to modify the data files that are included in the
fokker.dks file. Just modify the files in data_src with your favourite
image editor that understand the PCX format and then use the helper
script tools/build-data-from-source to regenerate contents of the
data/ directory. Build pcx2pgd first; the script looks for it in
build/ unless PCX2PGD points elsewhere.
